  "id": "fungiform-papillae",
  "term": "fungiform papillae",
  "definition": "Fungiform papillae are structures on the front part of the tongue that contain epithelial and connective tissues, nerve endings, and taste buds. In this context, they are relevant because their number and distribution differ across people and may be linked to differences in tongue sensation and perception.",
